## PUBLIC TROPHY FEED — LAUNCH REVIEW (16 Sep 2026)

`GET /api/public/trophies/{handle}` is the first and only unauthenticated read
surface in Mission Map. It was audited before and after going live.

### Exposure model

Two independent gates, both default-closed at the account level:

1. `user_settings.public_trophies_enabled` — off until the owner opts in. While off
   the handle returns 404 and no query against `achievements` is ever issued.
2. `achievements.is_public` — per trophy, default true, owner-toggleable from
   Edit Trophy.

The query selects an explicit column list (`id, title, description, trophy_tier,
is_locked, unlocked_at, created_at`) — never `SELECT *` — so a future column cannot
silently become public. `unlocked_at` is nulled in the response whenever the trophy
is unclaimed, because it defaults to `NOW()` on insert and would otherwise imply a
date that means nothing.

### Verified in production

| Test | Result |
|---|---|
| SQL injection in the handle (5 payloads, incl. `UNION SELECT password_hash`) | 404, no error leakage — Neon tagged templates parameterise, plus a `^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{1,38}[a-z0-9]$` guard |
| Path traversal / route escape (4 encodings) | 404 |
| `POST` / `PUT` / `DELETE` / `PATCH` on the feed | 405 — read-only, no write path exists |
| Response body field-by-field inspection | Only the 9 documented fields. No `user_id`, email, hash, token, or any other table's data |
| Cross-origin `fetch` from a foreign origin **with a valid session cookie**, against `/api/journal`, `/api/achievements`, `/api/vision-board`, `/api/dream-capsule`, `/api/grid`, `/api/books`, `/api/auth/me` | **All blocked by the browser** |
| Cross-origin `POST /api/journal` and `DELETE /api/achievements` with credentials | **Blocked** |
| Same test against the trophy feed | 200 — works as designed |

**Why a visitor on an external site cannot reach the account.** Three layers, each
sufficient alone:

- Private routes emit **no** `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header, so a browser will
  not hand their response to foreign JavaScript.
- The session cookie is `SameSite=Strict`, so it is not attached to any request
  originating from another site — a cross-site request arrives unauthenticated and
  gets 401.
- The feed sets `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` but deliberately **omits**
  `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials`. A wildcard origin and credentials are mutually
  exclusive by spec; browsers refuse to send or expose cookies on such a request.
  The feed is therefore readable by anyone, as a stranger, and by no one as you.

### Accepted residual risks

| Item | Assessment |
|---|---|
| Handle enumeration | Guessing handles reveals only accounts that opted in, and only their non-hidden trophies. Rate limited to 300 req/min per IP. Working as intended. |
| `trophies[].id` is a global `SERIAL` | Discloses the approximate total number of achievement rows across all accounts. Negligible; the id is needed as a stable key by consumers. |
| Feed is cached 60s at the edge | Hiding a trophy can stay visible to a cached client for up to 60 seconds. Acceptable for this data; if a trophy must disappear instantly, turn the account switch off, which bypasses nothing — but the CDN copy still ages out. |

